What is a REST API?

A REST API is used to communicate between the mobile app and the server.

The app sends a request and the server sends back data.

Example

In Cure Connect:

Flutter App
      ↓
Request Doctor List
      ↓
Server/API
      ↓
Doctor Data (JSON)
      ↓
Display in App
Common Methods
Method	Purpose
GET	Get data
POST	Create data
PUT	Update complete data
PATCH	Update partial data
DELETE	Delete data
Interview Answer

REST API is a way for a mobile application to communicate with a backend server. We use methods like GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE to fetch, create, update, and delete data.

WebSockets
What is WebSocket?

WebSocket provides a real-time connection between the app and the server.

Unlike REST API, the connection stays open.

Example

In a chat application:

User Sends Message
        ↓
WebSocket Connection
        ↓
Server
        ↓
Other User Receives Message Instantly

No need to refresh or call the API repeatedly.

REST API vs WebSocket
REST API	WebSocket
Request-Response	Continuous Connection
Connection closes after response	Connection stays open
Used for normal data fetching	Used for real-time updates
Less suitable for live chat	Best for live chat
